      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Mandelson security vetting scandal puts Starmer's leadership on the line",
      "summary": "Prime Minister Keir Starmer faced a parliamentary showdown and mounting resignation calls after it emerged that Peter Mandelson had failed security vetting before being appointed UK ambassador to Washington. Starmer sacked Foreign Office permanent secretary Olly Robbins, claiming he was kept in the dark, but opposition leaders \u2014 including Conservative leader Kemi Badenoch and all other major party chiefs \u2014 branded the explanation a lie or evidence of gross incompetence. Cabinet ministers including David Lammy and Liz Kendall rallied publicly behind Starmer over the weekend ahead of his Monday Commons statement.",
